\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Citing Slump In Fortnite, \uc2 Epic Games\uc2  Will Cut Jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael Levenson \par \uc2 715 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 March 2026\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The cut represents about 20 percent of the video game company's work force, a spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 The video game company \uc2 Epic Games\uc2  is laying off more than 1,000 employees, it said on Tuesday, citing a drop in the amount of time people are spending playing Fortnite.\par \par \uc2 ''The downturn in Fortnite engagement that started in 2025 means we're spending significantly more than we're making, and we have to make major cuts to keep the company funded,'' \uc2 Tim Sweeney\uc2 , the company's chief executive, wrote in a blog post. ''This layoff, together with over $500 million of identified cost savings in contracting, marketing and closing some open roles puts us in a more stable place.''\par \par \uc2 The cut represents about 20 percent of the work force at \uc2 Epic Games\uc2 , a company spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 It was the second time in recent years that the company, which is based in North Carolina, had announced major job cuts. In 2023, \uc2 Epic Games\uc2  laid off 830 employees, or about 16 percent of its work force, citing lower profit margins for Fortnite. ''I'm sorry we're here again,'' Mr. Sweeney wrote in his blog post.\par \par \uc2 Some of the challenges \uc2 Epic Games\uc2  is facing are problems for the wider video game industry, Mr. Sweeney wrote: Slower growth, weaker spending, a drop in sales of new video game consoles compared to the previous generation of consoles, and games ''competing for time against other increasingly engaging forms of entertainment.''\par \par \uc2 Some of the problems Epic faces are unique and related to Fortnite, the popular multiplayer shooting game released in 2017 that includes spinoffs like Lego Fortnite, Rocket Racing and Fortnite Festival.\par \par \uc2 ''Despite Fortnite remaining one of the most successful games in the world, we've had challenges delivering consistent Fortnite magic with every season; we're only in the early stages of returning to mobile and optimizing Fortnite for the world's billions of smartphones,'' Mr. Sweeney wrote.\par \par \uc2 Last year, \uc2 Apple\uc2  restored Fortnite to the App Store in the United States, nearly five years after \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  kicked it out of their app stores and \uc2 Epic Games\uc2  sued both companies in an antitrust case. \uc2 Epic Games\uc2  announced just days ago that Fortnite was back on \uc2 Google\uc2  Play.\par \par \uc2 While Fortnite is free to download, \uc2 Epic Games\uc2  said earlier this month that it was raising the price of V-Bucks, the in-game currency players can use to buy outfits, known as skins, and other accouterments. ''The cost of running Fortnite has gone up a lot and we're raising prices to help pay the bills,'' Epic said in announcing the price increase.\par \par \uc2 Despite its problems, Fortnite remains a popular game.\par \par \uc2 It led the United States in February among monthly active users of both PlayStation and Xbox, Mat Piscatella, a video game industry analyst at \uc2 Circana\uc2 , a market research firm, wrote in a post on social media, citing \uc2 Circana\uc2 's tracking data.\par \par \uc2 But there was a drop in engagement, the data showed. The average PlayStation user played Fortnite for 16 hours last month, down from 21 hours in February 2025, Mr. Piscatella wrote. Xbox users averaged 15 hours of Forntnite in February, down from 19 hours in February 2025.\par \par \uc2 Joost van Dreunen\uc2 , a market analyst and professor at \uc2 New York University\uc2 , said that Forntite must compete for attention not only with other popular games like \uc2 Roblox\uc2  but also with social media companies like \uc2 TikTok\uc2  and short-form videos on \uc2 YouTube\uc2  and other platforms.\par \par \uc2 Its problems, he said, are part of a broader shift in the industry, which is growing more in China than it is in the United States.\par \par \uc2 ''We're witnessing in real-time the decline of American cultural dominance in gaming,'' Mr. van Dreunen said. ''One of these landmarks like Fortnite is starting to feel the burn as the consumer entertainment industry is slowly moving from West to East in its financial gravity point.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Sweeney wrote that the workers who were laid off would receive a severance package that includes at least four months of base pay, with more based on tenure. \uc2 Epic Games\uc2  will also extend health care coverage for six months to U.S.-based employees who have been laid off, Mr. Sweeney wrote.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020260325em3p0004s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
