\par\par \uc2 Foreign Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Girl's Family Sues \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  Over Shooting In Canada\b0\par\par\uc2 By Vjosa Isai \par \uc2 639 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 March 2026\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The company banned the shooter's ChatGPT account but did not alert the authorities, a move that amounted to fatal negligence, the family claims.\par \par \uc2 The family of a student who was critically wounded during a mass shooting in British Columbia last month has sued the artificial intelligence company \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , accusing it of failing to warn the police of disturbing information about the shooter's ChatGPT account.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the family of the 12-year-old student, Maya Gebala, said she had been trying to lock a library door to protect her classmates when she was shot three times at close range, including once in the head. The girl remains hospitalized in Vancouver and has undergone multiple brain surgeries.\par \par \uc2 On Feb. 10, Jesse Van Rootselaar, 18, took two firearms from her home in Tumbler Ridge, British Columbia, and killed her mother and 11-year-old brother, the authorities said. She then traveled to the Tumbler Ridge Secondary School and killed five students and one educator and shot two other students, including Ms. Gebala.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Van Rootselaar died of a self-inflicted gunshot wound, the authorities said.\par \par \uc2 Eight months before the attack, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  had suspended a ChatGPT account associated with Ms. Van Rootselaar for violating its user agreement, the company said. She had documented her fascination with violence and weapons across several social media accounts, according to a review by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed on Monday by Ms. Gebala's mother, Cia Edmonds, claims that \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  was ''aware of the shooter's violent intentions'' and use of its A.I. chatbot to plan ''scenarios involving gun violence, including a mass casualty event.''\par \par \uc2 ''The purpose of this lawsuit is to learn the whole truth about how and why the Tumbler Ridge mass shooting happened,'' the law firm representing Ms. Gebala's family, Rice Parsons Leoni and Elliott LLP, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  said Ms. Van Rootselaar's account was suspended after messages from her ChatGPT chatbot account was detected by an automated system and manually reviewed by its team. The company did not provide more details about the contents of the messages.\par \par \uc2 While the company considered alerting officials in Canada, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  said it had ultimately decided that the messages did not meet its reporting threshold, which weighs whether there is imminent planning on the part of a user.\par \par \uc2 The company said it had considered the privacy of users when making referrals to law enforcement and did not want to distress them by involving the police.\par \par \uc2 Canada summoned top safety officials from \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  to Ottawa for a meeting in late February, after which the company revealed in a public letter that Ms. Van Rootselaar had created a second ChatGPT account when her other one was banned.\par \par \uc2 In the letter, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  said it had ''taken steps to strengthen our safeguards,'' including improving systems to detect banned users who try to establish new accounts and adding assessments by mental health and behavioral experts for complex cases.\par \par \uc2 David Eby\uc2 , the premier of British Columbia, said that the chief executive of \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , Sam Altman, had agreed to apologize to the community of Tumbler Ridge. \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  released a statement after they spoke on March 5.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Altman ''will work with them to find the best way to convey his apology and support to the Tumbler Ridge community,'' Jamie Radice, a spokeswoman for \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 After the shooting, Ms. Gebala and the other injured student were airlifted to the children's hospital in Vancouver, about 750 miles south of Tumbler Ridge.\par \par \uc2 The other student has since returned home, but Ms. Gebala's long-term prospects of recovery are uncertain.\par \par \uc2 The chief coroner of British Columbia has ordered a public inquest into the circumstances that led to the attack.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020260312em3c0003q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
