\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Fed Waits As It Eyes Uncertainty In Economy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Talmon Joseph Smith \par \uc2 594 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 January 2026\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Inflation is elevated but steady and the job market is holding up, leading economists to predict that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will keep interest rates at current levels.\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  officials meeting for the first time this year find themselves in a familiar place: torn by their dual mandates of price stability and full employment.\par \par \uc2 Far below its peak in 2022, inflation has nonetheless lingered above the central bank's 2 percent target for over four years. That has pushed officials to show they remain willing to keep money tight enough to cool price pressures in a growing economy that is absorbing the cost of new tariffs.\par \par \uc2 But the U.S. job market has slowed sharply, leading some to believe that the Fed may need to lower borrowing costs again this year to grease the wheels of commerce. Last year was the weakest since 2020 for employment growth, adding roughly a quarter of the estimated two million jobs that were added in 2024, and the second weakest since the global financial crisis in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Consumer sentiment readings have been dour, as households still find themselves squeezed by the increased cost of living.\par \par \uc2 Still, despite the decline in hiring momentum -- which has made job searches arduous for younger people and those who have been unemployed long-term -- overall unemployment is low by historical standards. In December 2024, the unemployment rate was 4.1 percent; that ticked up to 4.4 percent the next December.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers at the Fed ''are probably a little relieved after the latest batch of job market data,'' said Guy Berger, a labor economist. ''There's been some gradual cooling in the labor market but no sign that it's spiraling out of control.''\par \par \uc2 Other barometers of economic health are flashing green. Estimates of economic growth at the end of 2025 were strong. Leading U.S. banks, which reported robust earnings this month, expect that broad resilience to continue -- driven in part by a boom in artificial intelligence investments, and improvements in productivity as businesses appear to be boosting their efficiency.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration's changes in immigration policy have had an odd set of effects on the economy. Economists at \uc2 Vanguard\uc2 , the financial firm, estimate that demographic and immigration trends have accounted for 70 percent of the slowdown in payrolls growth. Yet analysts say the decline in newcomers seeking jobs has also very likely kept the unemployment rate contained.\par \par \uc2 The country is also aging, with waves of baby boomers retiring each month. This same demographic trend, however, has partly propped up the labor market, with many job seekers finding work in health care and social assistance, often serving older Americans.\par \par \uc2 Excluding the health care and social-assistance sector, which added about 700,000 jobs last year, private-sector job growth in 2025 was just over 20,000.\par \par \uc2 For now, most Fed officials are focusing on feeling for what they call ''the neutral rate'' -- the interest rate that would neither stimulate nor restrict commercial activity.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts believe that incoming stimulus from higher tax refunds -- the result of Congress's latest tax bill -- may speed up spending early this year. With inflation and employment hanging in this uncertain balance, most of Wall Street expected the Fed to pause before lowering rates any further.\par \par \uc2 ''In a stronger growth environment and with monetary policy now in the range of neutral-rate estimates, we anticipate the Fed will proceed with greater caution,'' said Josh Hirst, a senior economist at \uc2 Vanguard\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020260129em1t0004f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
